WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.296 --> 00:00:02.049
- Yeah, I heard it was Nazi G.I.

00:00:02.049 --> 00:00:02.425
That's a real script.

00:00:02.425 --> 00:00:04.672
- Oh, guys, guys, it's starting!

00:00:07.592 --> 00:00:09.937
Oh, oh my God, I thought I was on base.

00:00:09.937 --> 00:00:11.016
I was on the base here.

00:00:11.936 --> 00:00:12.647
(laughs)

00:00:12.647 --> 00:00:14.082
- Okay.

00:00:16.404 --> 00:00:21.404
(upbeat bugle music)

00:00:26.451 --> 00:00:28.204
- Uh, Minnesota, so far away.

00:00:28.204 --> 00:00:28.619
What about you?

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:29.826
Where are you from?

00:00:29.826 --> 00:00:31.231
- Well, define that.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.369
I mean, like, where was I born

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:33.785
or where did I live the longest

00:00:33.785 --> 00:00:35.461
or what place did I like the best?

00:00:37.453 --> 00:00:39.840
- Oh, C-141 taking off, you see that?

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.638
- It's Caroline. No, Caroline.

00:00:42.638 --> 00:00:45.505
"C", "C" as in Charlie Alpha Romeo Oscar.

00:00:45.505 --> 00:00:47.514
No, my name is not Charlie.

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:48.852
"C" as in Charlie.

00:00:48.852 --> 00:00:51.972
- That looks like a C-5 but
a C-5 is like, you know?

00:00:51.972 --> 00:00:54.306
- Where were you born I guess?

00:00:54.306 --> 00:00:55.850
- I was born in Guam,
but I only lived there

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:58.183
for like three months, so
it doesn't really count.

00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:00.064
And I mean, then I moved
to Germany, so, um,

00:01:00.064 --> 00:01:03.424
then I moved to Washington
state then Washington D.C.

00:01:18.573 --> 00:01:21.841
- Oh wow, this place is
almost as nice as the O Club.

00:01:22.881 --> 00:01:24.104
- What's the O Club?

00:01:24.104 --> 00:01:26.261
- Oh, the um, officer's club on base.

00:01:26.261 --> 00:01:27.678
It's kind of a big deal.

00:01:27.678 --> 00:01:30.638
- Texas, California, Northern California,

00:01:30.638 --> 00:01:32.136
and then Southern
California two years later

00:01:32.136 --> 00:01:33.854
but in between that I moved to Hawaii

00:01:33.854 --> 00:01:35.974
then we moved to Virginia.

00:01:36.347 --> 00:01:39.314
- Yeah, so even with this job
I still have like seven years

00:01:39.314 --> 00:01:41.601
until I can pay off my student debt.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.774
How about you?

00:01:42.774 --> 00:01:44.863
- Oh, I was actually on
the G.I. Bill in college.

00:01:44.863 --> 00:01:49.612
- Then Turkey, Okinawa in
Japan, Illinois, Oklahoma.

00:01:51.502 --> 00:01:53.370
- Oh my God, you're an
Air Force brat also?

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.659
- Yeah, oh my gosh!

00:01:54.659 --> 00:01:56.586
We must have been at
Ramstein at the same time.

00:01:56.586 --> 00:01:58.630
- Yeah, well I was stuck in
Patiala for like three months.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.334
- So by the time I turned
ten we moved to New Jersey

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:05.720
and I was able to get my first ID card.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:06.544
- I'm from Jersey.

00:02:06.544 --> 00:02:07.298
- Oh, you're from New Jersey?

00:02:07.298 --> 00:02:08.088
- Yeah, what part?

00:02:08.088 --> 00:02:09.548
- Oh, we were stationed at Fort Dix.

00:02:11.051 --> 00:02:12.557
I had so much fun at Fort Dix.

00:02:12.557 --> 00:02:14.391
It was awesome.

00:02:16.886 --> 00:02:19.339
It's an army base. Fort Dix.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.690
- An army base for dicks.

